  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 127 AM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nFor the weekend, some mid-level energy will remain in place which \nmay spark additional showers and storms each day, but the intensity \nof storms shouldn't be quite as high as it will be today and Friday. \nThe mid to upper level trough will get stuck over southwest Texas, \nresulting in those continued rain and storm chances. There may be \nsome lingering showers Monday morning, but by the afternoon, things \nlook dry across much of south central Texas. Essentially Monday \nthrough Wednesday of next week looks dry as weak zonal flow settles \nin over the region.",
